"district":"1","id":"H001082","name":"Rep. Hern, Kevin","original":false,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"OK"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-01-14","district":"7","id":"T000165","name":"Rep. Tiffany, Thomas P.","original":false,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"WI"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-01-14","district":"6","id":"C001118","name":"Rep. Cline, Ben","original":false,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"VA"}],"party_counts":{"R":84},"perspectives":[],"policy_area":"Civil Rights and Liberties, Minority Issues","related":{"companion":[],"related":[{"date":"2025-01-03","detail":"Related bill","id":null,"label":"H.Res. 5","title":"Adopting the Rules of the House of Representatives for the One Hundred Nineteenth Congress, and for other purposes.","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/5"}]},"selection":{"reason":"Impact scored and summarised by Gemini.","status":"analyzed"},"sources":{"latest":{"date":"2025-01-14","label":"Engrossed in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr28/BILLS-119hr28eh.htm"},"other":[{"label":"This bill on Congress.gov","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/28"}],"past":[{"date":"2025-01-03","label":"Introduced in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr28/BILLS-119hr28ih.htm"}]},"sponsor":{"chamber":"House","district":"17","id":"S001214","name":"Rep. Steube, W. Gregory","party":"R","state":"FL"},"stage":"passed_origin","stage_label":"Passed one chamber","summary":"The Protection of Women and Girls in Sports Act of 2025 aims to amend Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 to state that sex is determined solely by a person's reproductive biology and genetics at birth for athletic compliance. It prohibits federally funded educational athletic programs from allowing individuals whose sex at birth was male to participate in programs designated for women or girls. It also requires the Government Accountability Office to conduct a study on the impacts of male participation in single-sex sports for women and girls.","summary_detail":{"affected_groups":[{"effect":"Must ensure that athletic programs designated for women and girls do not permit individuals whose biological sex at birth was male to participate, in order to comply with Title IX.","group":"Educational institutions receiving federal financial assistance"},{"effect":"Will participate in sports programs where individuals whose sex at birth was male are barred from competing, and whose training practices are protected from female deprivation of benefits.","group":"Female athletes in federally funded programs"},{"effect":"Are prohibited from participating in athletic programs or activities designated for women or girls, though training and practicing is permitted under specific conditions.","group":"Male athletes whose biological sex at birth was male"}],"key_provisions":["Defines sex for Title IX athletics compliance as being based solely on a person's reproductive biology and genetics at birth.","Prohibits recipients of federal financial assistance from allowing individuals of the male sex to participate in athletic programs designated for women or girls.","Allows males to train or practice with women's or girls' programs only if no female is deprived of a roster spot, competition opportunity, scholarship, admission, or other benefit.","Directs the Comptroller General to carry out a study and submit a report on the benefits lost by women and girls in single-sex sports due to male participation, including negative psychological, developmental, participatory, and sociological effects."],"missing_information":["Specific penalties or enforcement mechanisms for educational institutions that violate the new Title IX provision.","Timeline or deadline for the Comptroller General to complete and submit the required study and report."],"plain_summary":"The Protection of Women and Girls in Sports Act of 2025 aims to amend Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 to state that sex is determined solely by a person's reproductive biology and genetics at birth for athletic compliance. It prohibits federally funded educational athletic programs from allowing individuals whose sex at birth was male to participate in programs designated for women or girls. It also requires the Government Accountability Office to conduct a study on the impacts of male participation in single-sex sports for women and girls.","significance":"The bill alters federal standards under Title IX regarding sex-segregated athletics by establishing a biological definition at birth, impacting all federally funded educational institutions and their sports programs."},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-27T13:33:01+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr28/BILLS-119hr28eh.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"Protection of Women and Girls in Sports Act of 2025","viability":64.3,"viability_detail":{"breakdown":[{"available":true,"effective_weight":35.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Detected stage","value":"Passed one chamber"}],"key":"stage","label":"Legislative stage","note":"Stage value from the table on the About page.","points":28.0,"value":0.8,"weight":35},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Committee activity","value":"Reported out of committee (or past committee stage)"}],"key":"committee","label":"Committee activity","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Floor activity","value":"Passed a chamber"}],"key":"floor","label":"Floor consideration","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Days since latest action","value":649},{"label":"Half-life (days)","value":90}],"key":"momentum","label":"Recent action","note":"","points":0.1,"value":0.0067,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":10.0,"inputs":[{"la